{"body":{"text":["Well, the address and the buffer are stores. So I don't know why they should be shipped with the site, but they're not stores, they're integrations perhaps. Um, no, I guess the buffer is a store. I don't know if that means that we should rename the stores directory or we should have one that is stores and one that is called integrations and then put the address in there. And for the site, there seems to be various files that just import and export directly as placeholder files. I get that might be the case, so that there may be separate files for loading because they are to be loaded into workers, but perhaps then they could be put in a directory so they're not confused with what the site actually is, because they're really just imports, right? And please, I haven't read the address, but please just review it, that it's, written upon our principles, etc., because it's really quite a functional thing. No, I don't say that the helper shouldn't be there because I reject it. I reject the unnecessary using of helpers inside components because I found it completely unnecessary. But we've already established that the chassis has nothing to do with lots of the things that have to do with rendering. And if it's a global thing, then maybe fine. But the chassis is supposed to be able to go with various types of UI implementation, so it's agnostic. So if that is by nature the case, then allowing that decoupling is actually honoring its nature, right? So that's my reasoning. And what's your response to that then? Not saying I'm right, but that's my values, and I want you to hold those values in your reasoning. Well, yeah, the point is, for point number 4, is that we were going to use Git for that in the next step, but just do something pragmatic for now. And at least we can move in that direction. And then when we do Git, but it's a later step. Still want to clean this up first."]},"id":"1M87MKJCECE600R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
